# `right[at]` off a parameter written `right: Float64Array` (undefined, null or the view by its type) asks for an object and reads: it is typed without a guess, so nobody guesses at `right`. The row of the loop takes it among
# its views all the same, and the front, finding no guess at it and no proven view, asked it whether it is an Array: false by its type, so the typed copy was swept and the copy built for size was the loop: `left.length` by name in every turn.
# The front asks a view for its own class. Two heads: the typed copy and the other one.
# RUN(PAIR): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# PAIR: = TypeTest v1 testedType=Float64Array
# PAIR-COUNT-2: isLoopHead=true
# PAIR-NOT: isLoopHead=true
# RUN(PAIRWHOLE): walk f1 mechanisms=all
# PAIRWHOLE-NOT: testedType=Array
# The same where the turns store, and over bytes.
# RUN(STORES): walk f2 mechanisms=all
# STORES: = TypeTest v2 testedType=Float64Array
# STORES-COUNT-2: isLoopHead=true
# STORES-NOT: isLoopHead=true
