# BYTES: = TypeTest v1 testedType=Uint8Array
# BYTES-COUNT-2: isLoopHead=true
# BYTES-NOT: isLoopHead=true
# A const read off a field in front of the loops, as everybody writes it: the field may be undefined by its type, for the arrow is made before the constructor fills it.
# RUN(CONST): walk f37 mechanisms=all
# CONST-NOT: testedType=Array
# RUN(CONSTASKED): walk f37 mechanisms=all
# CONSTASKED: = TypeTest {{*}} testedType=Float64Array
# RUN(NAMES): walk f38 mechanisms=all
# NAMES-NOT: testedType=Array
# Nothing in the place of the view throws in the first turn and not in front of it; a shorter view, one that has lost its memory, one whose memory shrinks and grows between the calls, an instance of a class below, a view with a `length` of its own, two views over one memory.
